# Idle Laboratory — Cursor / Bugbot rules (index)

Detailed standards live in **[`.cursor/rules/`](.cursor/rules/)** (MDC rules picked up by Cursor Agent and GitHub Bugbot).

Project overview and architecture: **[`README.md`](README.md)**.

## Must follow (summary)

1. **Layers:** UI → BLoC → **Service** (RxDart) → Repository → SharedPreferences. No remote DB clients.
2. **Heavy logic in Services**, not BLoCs. Repositories = persistence only (`guardAsync`, `StorageKeys`).
3. **Performance:** `BlocSelector`, visibility-gated subscriptions, throttle hot streams, timers in services.
4. **UI:** `AppLayoutBloc` / `AppVersionEnum`; no `screen_util`; no hardcoded user strings (`context.l10n`).
5. **Prestige:** lifetime stats survive; flush saves on prestige / pause / dispose; do not pause playtime on `inactive`.
6. **Forms / pagination:** when those UI types appear, follow `.cursor/rules/forms-and-lists.mdc`.

When rules conflict with legacy code, improve incrementally toward these standards — do not big-bang rewrite unrelated tabs.
